      What is E-commerce:
        The term e-commerce refers to a business concept that enables organisations and people to buy and sell commodities and services on the Internet. Ecommerce is available through a computer, tablet, smartphone, and other intelligent devices in four primary market sectors
        Business to Business (B2B):Alibaba,IndiaMart
		Business to Consumer (B2C):Amazon,Flipkart
		Consumer to Consumer (C2C):eBay
		Consumer to Business (C2B)
 2.Why magento2
 	  Magento 2 was developed to address the limitations of Magento 1 and to meet the rapidly evolving, high-performance needs of modern e-commerce.
   	  Magento 2 is compatible with the latest technologies such as PHP7 which means faster load time in comparison to Magento 1.
	  EASIER CHECK-OUT PROCESS:n Magento 2, the check-out process consists of only two quick steps, allowing clients to do better shopping and reduce cart erosion. It gives guest check-out options without login or registration.
	  The Magento 2 administration interface is easier to use and easier to operate. It is very adaptable and created so that administrators can easily access relevant data and easily manage goods. This contributes to reducing time in the administration of a shop online and is very useful.
	  It enables several integrated payment gateway methods such as Paypal, Google Checkouts, Braintree, etc.
3.Which type of project created in magento2
      	Large-scale B2C Fashion & Luxury Retailers: Websites requiring high-resolution visuals, complex product configurations, and personalized experiences (e.g., clothing, footwear, jewelry).
		Complex B2B Wholesale Portals: Platforms designed for manufacturers or distributors with tiered pricing, bulk ordering, and specific customer group access.
		International/Multi-Storefront Operations: Brands selling across multiple countries, using different languages and currencies under one backend.
		Headless Commerce Solutions: High-performance, fast-loading stores using PWA (Progressive Web Application) frontends (like Hyvä, ScandiPWA, or Vue Storefront) with Magento in the backend.
		Automotive & Electronics Accessories: Stores with extensive catalogs, advanced filtering, and bundle products (e.g., selling car parts or home electronics). 
